    "title": "pandas.describe_option — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.describe_option#\n\n- \npandas.describe_option(*pat=''* ,*_print_desc=True* )[source]#\n- Print the description for one or more registered options. Call with no arguments to get a listing for all registered options. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **pat** str, default “”\n    - String or string regexp pattern. Empty string will return all options. For regexp strings, all matching keys will have their description displayed.\n    - **_print_desc** bool, default True\n    - If True (default) the description(s) will be printed to stdout. Otherwise, the description(s) will be returned as a string (for testing).\n  - Returns:\n    - None\n    - If `_print_desc=True` .\n    - str\n    - If the description(s) as a string if `_print_desc=False` .\n See also \n  - `get_option`\n  - Retrieve the value of the specified option.\n  - `set_option`\n  - Set the value of the specified option or options.\n  - `reset_option`\n  - Reset one or more options to their default value.\n Notes For all available options, please view the User Guide. Examples >>> pd.describe_option(\"display.max_columns\") display.max_columns : int If max_cols is exceeded, switch to truncate view...",
